<title>USA: Western U.S. Midwest turns colder, no frost seen.</title>
<headline>Western U.S. Midwest turns colder, no frost seen.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Temperatures dropped into the low- to mid-40s Farenheit across parts of the western U.S. Midwest Wednesday night with some 30s F reported in North Dakota, Weather Services Corp said.</p>
<p>&quot;It's rather chilly but it's not frost by any means,&quot; said meteorologist Joel Burgio.</p>
<p>However, freezing temperatures were reported Tuesday night in Williston, North Dakota, he said. The freeze was about two weeks ahead of the normal date.</p>
<p>No freezing temperatures were expected in the corn belt through the weekend, Burgio said.</p>
<p>--Emily Kaiser 312-408-8749</p>
